EXT. WINDMILL RANCH, DRY PLAINS - DAY

A tall steel windmill creaks against a bleached sky. A sagging fence runs off into dust. Beneath the tower, a water trough, half-empty.

ABEL MONTGOMERY-OSEI (50s, long coat, sun-cracked hat, a face like riverbed) rides in, dismounts, and loosens the cinch. His horse drinks. He doesn't.

He walks to the windmill. Reaches into the shadow of the tower and pulls out a tin box. Opens it. Inside: a folded letter, a photograph, a wedding ring.

He reads the letter. Folds it. Pockets the ring. Holds the photograph a long time.

Then he sits against the windmill leg and stares across the plain.

A faint crackle from his saddlebag. A small battered radio, strapped there for emergencies.

ABEL
(to the radio)
Not now.

The crackle repeats. A voice, thin and far:

RADIO (V.O.)
Abel. You there?

ABEL
(sighing)
I'm here.

RADIO (V.O.)
They found the bodies at Cutter's Rise.

ABEL
I know.

RADIO (V.O.)
It was the Calloway gang.

ABEL
I know who it was.

RADIO (V.O.)
What are you going to do?

Abel looks at the windmill blades turning. Looks at the dust.

ABEL
I'm going to stay here a while.

RADIO (V.O.)
Abel--

ABEL
A while.

He clicks the radio off. Puts it back in the bag. The wind picks up. The windmill groans.

Far on the horizon, three riders appear as dark specks. Abel doesn't turn.

ABEL (CONT'D)
(to himself)
Took you long enough.

He stands. Draws his revolver. Checks it. Holsters it. Then, deliberately, he sits down again and takes off his hat, resting it on his knee.

The riders grow. Abel waits.

At two hundred yards, one of them raises a rifle. Abel doesn't flinch.

ABEL (CONT'D)
(softly, to the photograph)
Not yet.

The shot cracks. The photograph leaps from his hand, a hole through the corner. He stares at it. Then he is on his feet, gun up, firing three times at the riders. One falls. The others scatter into the dust.

Silence returns. The windmill creaks. Abel crosses to the photograph, bends, and picks it up with great care. A hole where a shoulder used to be.

He lowers himself to the ground. Breathes.

ABEL (CONT'D)
(to the sky)
There. Now we're done.

The wind carries the smoke away. The blades keep turning.
